                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-01T11:00:00+08:00">July 1, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 1—10:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>523. Legation’s 510, June 27, 10 p.m. Commander in Chief on June 29th directed U.
                    S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Barker</hi> to proceed to Foochow and to report on
                    conditions there.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
